{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "Canonical Category -> Subcategory taxonomy (stable domain model), the single source of truth for the validators AND the backend -- TaxonomyService loads this file at startup, so no Java service holds a hardcoded copy of the vocabulary any more. Navigation groups are NOT here -- they live in a separate presentation artifact (navigation.json), so the domain model stays stable when navigation changes or is later generated. EDITORIAL CLASSIFICATION DRIVES NAVIGATION: a topic gathers CivicContent whose subcategory == the topic, and a category gathers CivicContent whose category_tags contain its label. Descriptive 'tags' are NEVER used to place content in the hierarchy -- they serve search, filtering and AI enrichment only, and cross-category relationships are an enrichment product persisted as metadata, not a second editorial taxonomy. 'matchCategories' are the raw source-data category strings that map to this display category; 'matchCategoryTags' are the canonical editorial category_tags that associate any CivicContent item with it. Every source -- Resources, News, RSS/Laws, Flyers and Expert content -- classifies into THIS vocabulary; upstream label drift is normalized at the source, not compensated for by widening these lists (Decision 032).",
